  // piece is clamped into its string before it is used (kube.uproc's
  // `i + (n + 1) * (1 - least(1, i + 1))` is `n` when `i` is -1), and the
  // lifetime is tested as digits (`replace` each away, on at most 12
  // characters) before anything reads it as a number. Substrings are views:
  // nothing copies the answer, which may be as large as a record, into the
  // 512 bytes of scratch a decision has. Each piece is bound once
  // (`cel.bind`) — written out at every use, this decision was 12 KB of the
  // 256 KiB a whole graph's config may be.
